amux daemon — run or control the local daemon (restart loads a new binary)

usage: amux daemon [<command>]

The daemon owns the store and the agent engine: it hosts every running agent,
so stopping or restarting it stops the agents it hosts. Bare amux daemon runs
one in the foreground until signalled (what auto-launch spawns); the commands
below control a detached one.

commands:
  stop     stop the running daemon cleanly
  start    start a detached daemon if none is answering
  restart  stop, then start: how a newly installed binary is loaded

Run 'amux daemon <command> --help' for details.
